{
  "format": 1,
  "notes": "Masses kg, lengths m, thrust N, Isp s, torque N m. Shapes are frustums: radius at the top and bottom, height; a part's origin is the center of its bottom. Tanks hold kerosene and liquid oxygen (~1,030 kg/m3 together). Kinds: command (needed to fly), tank, engine, decoupler (drops what is below it), parachute, structure (adapters, nose cones). max_temperature: K a part's skin stands (default 1400); a heat shield under a capsule stands ~3300 for coming in from orbit or the Moon. experiment: what science a part does (id, name, value, situations: landed / flying / space_low / space_high; needs_air; maps: maps the ground from orbit). crew: people aboard (crewed vessels fly without a link home). antenna_range: m from home the part's antenna still links (built into command parts: ~the Moon). cost: $ millions. isru: a propellant plant: kg a day it makes landed on ice (rate_ice) or in a usable air (rate_air). docking: a docking port (at a stack's top or bottom). rcs_thrust: N of translation thrust (docking). side: a side docking port, put on a radial group: it faces straight out from the core; a plain stack docks to it and hangs off it. Power (W and Wh): battery: Wh it stores; power_draw: W it draws all the time (avionics, life support, an instrument, a transmitter); wheel_power: W its reaction wheels draw turning hard; experiment energy: Wh a run takes; isru power: W the plant draws running; generator: W made day and night (an RTG, a reactor); solar: wings unfolding from it (power: W at 1 AU square to the Sun, length and width m of each wing, wings: 2 out both sides of a stack part, 1 straight out from a radial copy). Kind power: batteries, solar wings, generators. Kind legs: landing legs (legs: span, m their pads stand out beyond the mount when down; crash_speed: what landing on them stands), on a radial group; G lowers them. Propellants (vessel/propellants.py): a tank's propellant_type and an engine's propellant are one of kerolox (the default), methalox, hydrolox, hypergolic; an engine burns only tanks of its own kind in its section. Cryogenic propellants boil off in sunlight (hydrolox fastest); insulation scales a tank's boil-off; cooling: kg of cryogenic propellant a cryocooler keeps from boiling (while powered). Life (vessel/life.py): supplies: kg of oxygen, water and food it holds (in its mass; 5 kg a person a day); recycling: the share its life support recycles while powered; shielding: the share of radiation that gets through (1: all).",
